                <pb facs="0527" n="434" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg434"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2131/284: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Colombia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-08T12:00:00-05:00">February 8,
                        1935—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>13. Department’s No. 5, January 24, 8 p.m. The Department is gratified to learn
                    from your telegram No. 19 of February 5, 10 a.m.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d454-f1"/>
                    that the Colombian Government plans to expedite conclusion of Trade Agreement.
                    Has the Government indicated any modifications or suggestions with respect to
                    the draft agreement or intimated whether it desires the Department to send an
                    expert to Bogotá?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
